  "headline": "Ghana initiates discussions with Russia for first nuclear power station",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "President John Dramani Mahama has disclosed that Ghana has initiated discussions with Russia’s State Nuclear Energy Corporation, Rosatom, regarding the establishment of the country’s first nuclear power station. Speaking at the Third Russia-Africa Summit in Moscow on October 29, 2026, Mahama stated that Ghana is pursuing a diversified energy mix, including renewables, while advancing foundations for the peaceful use of nuclear energy. He noted that the Soviet Union previously provided Ghana with a two-megawatt nuclear reactor for research purposes in 1964."
